  "reason": "The current best (config_049: scvi_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.7250, and we have strong evidence that image encoder (ViT-L > ResNet50), aggregation (transformer > avgpool), and weighted fusion all contribute to performance. However, the RNA encoder choice remains underexplored at the top of the performance range: we've only tested pca_n2000 and scvi_n200, with a small gap (~1.3%) between them. config_043 (scgpt, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_049, isolating the effect of the scgpt RNA encoder in the context of the strongest image pipeline. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it identifies a new promising representation axis to exploit; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA encoder and redirects budget toward other axes (e.g., profile setting or fusion refinement). This is the most informative next step because the RNA encoder is a fundamental representation choice, the comparison is controlled (only one variable changes), and the outcome directly determines whether further RNA-encoder exploration is warranted under the limited budget."
